s/saierXP","html_url":"https://github.com/saierXP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T06:19:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T16:00:02Z","body":"I happened to discover that can reproduce the problem **100%**.\n\nI used the `Spacedesk` software to connect my tablet via USB to copy the screen. When the tablet entered the software and started copying, the main monitor went black. After it turn on, the Godot screen was offset.\n\n**Edit: The problem cannot be reproduced by connecting a physical monitor to the laptop, which could also be due to the laptop's graphics card being too old.**\n\n**Edit2: \nChanging the screen refresh rate in Windows settings can also trigger this issue. This will make the screen going black and then back to normal, similar to Spacedesk simulating a table connected as an extended screen.\nChanging resolution and scale can't make screen offset.**\n\nThe offset y should be equal to the height of the window title bar, which is `29` pixels.\n\nAdditionally, OpenGL cannot reproduce this, but Vulkan and DX12 can.\n\nWhen I asked the AI, it said that `DXGI` + `DWM` was not synchronizing the client area information in the window.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5406364933/reactions","total_coun